  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"This edition consists of 600 copies on Mowhawk [sic] Superfine set in Times and printed on a Hamada 800 offset press by Brad Freeman, master printer at Pyramid Atlantic, under the direction of Elizabeth Whiteley, book artist, of which copies are numbered 1-100 and signed by the author and the book artist, and 500 copies are numbered from 101 to 600 ..."--Colophon card.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">The loose sheets are cut to resemble a deck of playing cards and are printed with the text on the obverse and illustrations on the reverse in playing-card fashion. Cards can be "shuffled" to provide multiple and varied readings.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Issued in paper box with clear plastic lid.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"As the title suggests, this oversized deck of cards, containing 52 chapters based on the interactions of five characters, can be shuffled and dealt (read) in any order. The loose sheets are cut to resemble a deck of playing cards and are printed with the text on the obverse and illustrations on the reverse in playing-card fashion. The illustrations, done in collaboration, have their own shuffled collage-like look. A neat production. References: Johanna Drucker, The Century of Artists' Books, 1995."</subfield>
    <subfield code="c">Printed Matter.</subfield>
  </datafield>
